{%- comment -%}
  cart.js defines <cart-items>, <cart-remove-button>, <cart-note>,
  <discount-code> and <shipping-calculator>. The cart page used to be the only
  thing that loaded it, but every one of those elements also renders inside the
  drawer, which is on every page -- so the drawer's quantity steppers, remove
  buttons, note, discount field and shipping estimate were all inert markup
  everywhere except /cart. Loaded from the header, it is present on every page,
  and main-cart-items no longer loads it a second time (a second execution
  would throw on the repeated customElements.define).
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'cart.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- comment -%}
  Safety net: any add-to-cart form that is not owned by <product-form> would
  otherwise post natively and get redirected to /cart. Loaded here, beside
  cart.js, so it is present on every page.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'cart-add-interceptor.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
